      "mergeID": "604e0c30f3d62e608af2fb93",
      "mergedPostDetails": "About two hours after entering the world, the other player's avatar frame drop happen. I've tried reinstalling the game, erasing all of the cache, changing the resolution, changing the installation path of the game, and trying many things, but it doesn't go back to the way it was. The problem occurred about a month ago, and after about two hours in one world, only the movement of other players, not the game itself, seems to be cut off. The strange thing about this is that the movement of desktop users seems to be cut off, but the movement of VR users seems quite smooth. Instead of a frame drop of the game itself, it makes a movement that is likely to be seen when there is a network problem. (I've tested it with different games, but I don't see any problems with graphics cards, memory, CPUs, or networks. Reconnect to the world make this issue to be fine for about 2 hours, but again it continue over and over. I don't know the cause, and I'm a Korean user, but there's no any information about this issue in Korea VRChat forum, so I post my issue here to get answer.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Other player's avatar frame drop.",
