      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ca74f3fb98a820b3ffec9cf|full_name}: There was an older bug where players who were in an instance for a long time (4+ hours) would have jerky movement (in that case, the remote player has to rejoin to fix it).\nIn the bug I reported here, it can occur after only tens of minutes, and is fixed - or at least shuffled so different people have jerky movement - when the viewing/local player rejoins.",
