      "statusChangeID": "60f71bcf801aaa23dec5327d",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "complete",
      "value": "In 2021.3.1, we made some (pretty sweeping!) network changes that should help mitigate or prevent this issue entirely.\nWe haven't observed this issue ourselves, nor have we seen verifiable reports of the issue since the release. As such, I'm marking this as Complete.\n**Notably, this is the issue we've addressed:** In a given instance with a number of users present, one or more users would eventually begin to exhibit IK \"slideshowing\", where IK update rate would slow down a lot and interpolation between IK updates would break or only have one interim step. This behavior would be observed by everyone in the instance on the same person-- in other words, if Person A was in this failure state, Persons B, C, D, etc would *all* see the behavior.\nIf you are observing other IK issues but they do not match the above description, *please create a new Feedback post.*",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
